From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: settings for the device's other drives

cros-disks (NickelOS patch 0002) mounts the volume that holds Windows read-
only and hides other systems' own partitions. This lets the user choose,
per drive of the device's other internal disks (by filesystem UUID), in
Settings > Device > Storage management > Other drives:

- Show in Files: off keeps the drive unmounted, now and at every sign-in
  (pref nickel.drives_not_shown).
- Allow changes, for an NTFS drive that came up read-only (Windows' own
  volume, or one Windows left hibernated): after a dialog about Windows'
  Fast Startup, the volume is mounted again writable, now and at every
  sign-in (pref nickel.windows_drives_writable; VolumeManager passes the
  mount option nickel-windows-writable, which cros-disks takes out). A
  volume Windows left hibernated stays read-only, as ntfs-3g decides, and
  the setting says why.

StorageHandler sends the drives (onNickelDrivesUpdated) with their mount
state, as cros-disks reported it, so Chrome never looks into a drive.

